WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.960
Sonic is back with a new friend and a new
foe in "Sonic the Hedgehog 2" – and a familiar

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.030
voice is bringing the blue blur's new friend
Tails to life on the big screen.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.269
Here's everything else you need to know before
you see "Sonic the Hedgehog 2."

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:16.370
"Let's do this."

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:21.699
Even after it was almost derailed by a set
of eerily human-looking teeth, the film adaptation

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:27.150
of Sega's beloved mascot was a hit both with
fans of the games and at the box office, earning

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.189
nearly $320 million worldwide.

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:34.210
Although critics felt there was some room
for improvement, the zippy design of Sonic

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:38.670
himself and the likable cast of human characters
were enough to have the film declared the

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.820
rare successful video game adaptation.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.210
Just three months after the release of the
first movie, Variety confirmed that "Sonic

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.890
the Hedgehog 2" was officially on the way,
with director Jeff Fowler and screenwriters

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.510
Pat Casey and Josh Miller all returning.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:58.589
In the first film, we're introduced to Sonic,
an alien hedgehog who uses a dimension-bending

00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:00.220
ring to travel to earth.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:06.330
Once there, he's pursued by the evil Dr. Robotnik,
who wants to harness Sonic's supersonic speed

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.980
for use in his robotics experiments.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:14.720
Sonic teams up with Sheriff Tom and his wife
Maddie in order to evade Dr. Robotnik's increasingly

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.180
menacing attempts to capture the hedgehog.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.270
"Sonic the Hedgehog" was enjoyable and did
justice to the games, but it also left lots

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.390
of room to go bigger and better with another
installment.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:29.400
Now that we know one is on the way, let's
dig into the details of what we know about

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.800
the release date, cast, and plot of the upcoming
"Sonic the Hedgehog 2."

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.210
When Paramount made the announcement about
the sequel, it was just that: news and not

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.210
much else.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:44.510
However, in late July 2020, the studio revealed
the official release date for "Sonic the Hedgehog

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:45.510
2."

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:49.420
Ben Schwartz, who voices the speedy little
hedgehog, posted to his Twitter account a

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.820
video of himself confirming the news.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:57.210
The video simply featured Schwartz strolling
beside massive promotional posters for "Sonic

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.390
the Hedgehog" while awkwardly explaining what
he was seeing.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:05.550
The caption of the video is where the actor
made things crystal clear: "SONIC 2 IS OFFICIALLY

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.860
COMING 2 THEATERS 4/8/22!!"

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.550
One of the biggest strengths of the first
"Sonic the Hedgehog" was its cast.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:17.340
Ben Schwartz, best known for "Parks and Recreation"
and "The Afterparty," and an avowed fan of

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.220
the original Sonic games, gave an energetic
vocal performance as the titular hedgehog.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:27.500
Jim Carrey was delightfully unhinged as the
villainous Dr. Robotnik, while James Marsden

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.810
and Tika Sumpter provided the right balance
of humor and heart as Sonic's unassuming human

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:33.810
allies.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.050
All four actors will reprise their roles in
"Sonic the Hedgehog 2.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:41.250
Colleen O'Shaughnessy, who voiced Tails in
the Sonic games, performed the character's

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.160
dialogue in a brief, post-credits sequence.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.000
That set up Tails to be a much more prominent
part of the next film, and O'Shaughnessy will

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.000
return.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.370
There are two new big names in the cast of
"Sonic the Hedgehog 2."

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:59.090
In June 2021, Shemar Moore, well known for
his work on CBS procedurals "Criminal Minds"

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.500
and "S.W.A.T.," posted to Instagram a picture
of himself on the "Sonic 2" set with the other

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.610
primary members of the human cast.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:09.740
He announced his casting, but didn't reveal
any details about his character.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:14.210
However, Moore briefly appears in a scene
in the third "Sonic the Hedgehog 2" trailer.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:21.180
In August 2021, Variety reported that Emmy-and-Oscar-nominated
superstar Idris Elba had joined "Sonic the

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:26.910
Hedgehog 2" as the voice of Knuckles, a Sonic
adversary-turned-ally in the '90s Sega games.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:32.209
During the 2021 Game Awards, "Sonic the Hedgehog
2" voice actor Ben Schwartz introduced the

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:36.960
first trailer for the film, with a second
teaser arriving in time for the 2022 Super

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.960
Bowl.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.770
Both clips revealed a few details about the
plot of the highly anticipated sequel.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:46.720
After Sonic blasted away Dr. Robotnik to a
mushroom planet in the first film, he was

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.720
determined to escape his prison and return
to Earth.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.500
As revealed in the third trailer, which hit
the internet on March 14th, Dr. Robotnik returns

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.520
to wreak more havoc, and he's in possession
of a giant green emerald, which he proclaims

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.530
to be "the source of ultimate power."

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:06.690
Sonic, after crashing through a ring portal
on a pile of snow, rudely interrupting a Hawaiian

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:11.959
destination wedding, announces his intention
to stop his persistent nemesis — or otherwise,

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:13.550
"the world is doomed."

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.030
Neither side is alone in their quest this
time.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:21.560
Dr. Robotik has brought along the destructive
and nefarious echidna Knuckles, while Sonic

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.479
has Tails fighting in his corner.

00:04:23.479 --> 00:04:27.389
Overall, the "Sonic" sequel looks like it
has much more in common with the games that

00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:32.639
inspired the movie, with familiar faces on
a new adventure hopefully everyone will love.

